        {"en": "they", "es": "ellos, ellas", "pos": "pron", "ex_en": "They are my friends.", "ex_es": "Ellos son mis amigos."},
        {"en": "is", "es": "es, está", "pos": "verb", "ex_en": "Luis is tired.", "ex_es": "Luis está cansado."},
        {"en": "are", "es": "eres, son, están", "pos": "verb", "ex_en": "Are you okay?", "ex_es": "¿Estás bien?"},
        {"en": "not", "es": "no", "pos": "adv", "ex_en": "I'm not tired.", "ex_es": "No estoy cansado."}
      ],
      "sentences": [
        {"en": "He's my friend Tom.", "es": "Él es mi amigo Tom."},
        {"en": "She's a teacher, not a student.", "es": "Ella es maestra, no estudiante."},
        {"en": "We're students. Are you a teacher?", "es": "Somos estudiantes. ¿Tú eres maestro?"},
        {"en": "They aren't tired. They're great!", "es": "No están cansados. ¡Están muy bien!"},
        {"en": "What is it? It's a number.", "es": "¿Qué es? Es un número."}
      ],
      "tip_es": "Formas cortas: he's, she's, it's, we're, they're. Para negar agrega not: he isn't, we aren't. En inglés nunca se omite el sujeto, así que es maestra se dice she's a teacher."
